## Phase 1 -- Chroma Key Engine

> Read `jonathaniscarroll/living-characters/readme.md`. Then create `scripts/chroma.js` as a standalone module with no external dependencies.
>
> It must export three functions:
>
> **`chromaKey(imageDataUrl, options) → Promise<dataUrl>`**
> Draws the image onto an offscreen canvas, iterates every pixel, converts RGB → HSL, and for each pixel:
> - If hue is within `options.tolerance` of `options.h` (0–360) AND saturation > 0.2 → set alpha to 0
> - If hue is within `options.tolerance + options.spill` of `options.h` → lerp alpha from 0→255 (soft fringe) and suppress green spill by shifting the green channel toward the average of red and blue
> - Otherwise leave pixel unchanged
> Returns a transparent-background PNG dataURL.
> Default options: `{ h: 120, tolerance: 0.35, spill: 0.15 }`
>
> **`chromaKeyCanvas(sourceCanvas, options) → HTMLCanvasElement`**
> Same algorithm but accepts an already-drawn canvas and returns a new canvas.
>
> **`sampleHue(imageDataUrl, x, y) → Promise<number>`**
> Draws the image, reads the pixel at (x, y), converts to HSL, returns the hue (0–360).
>
> Include the RGB→HSL conversion inline (no imports). Expose all three on `window.lcChroma` and as ES module exports.
